.Rproj.user
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
/.quarto/

**/*.quarto_ipynb
/*.html

# Quarto build byproducts left in the source tree (the real copies live in _site/)
/hand-on-ex/**/*_files/
/in-class-ex/**/*_files/

# Take-home Exercise 1 (see take-home-ex/take-home-ex1/scripts/ for the pipeline)
/take-home-ex/**/*_files/
# Monte-Carlo results: seeded, so a recomputation reproduces them exactly
take-home-ex/take-home-ex1/data/cache/
# Bulk source data that can be re-downloaded from a stable URL. The analysed
# FIRMS CSV and the OSM extracts ARE committed: the FIRMS open archive is a
# rolling 7-day window, so those exact records cannot be recovered.
take-home-ex/take-home-ex1/data/raw/idn_cod_ab/
take-home-ex/take-home-ex1/data/raw/*_SouthEast_Asia_7d.csv
take-home-ex/take-home-ex1/data/raw/geoBoundaries-*.geojson

# FIRMS API credentials. scripts/01_download_firms.R reads the key from here
# or from the FIRMS_MAP_KEY environment variable; neither belongs in the repo.
.firms_key
*.key
.env

# Intermediates Quarto leaves behind when a render is interrupted. A stray one
# of these once became a 13th project input and broke the build, which is what
# `render: ["**/*.qmd"]` in _quarto.yml now guards against; ignoring them keeps
# them out of the repo as well. Nothing here is a source file.
**/*.rmarkdown
# Freeze output. Freeze is not enabled for this project, so anything Quarto
# writes here is a byproduct; the real copies live in _site/.
/_freeze/
